getAssignedWorker [SimTalk]
Returns the assigned Worker designated by the number in the WorkerPool designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.getAssignedWorker(No:integer) -> object
Parameter
The parameter No of data type integer designates the number of the Worker that is assigned.
Return Value
The return value has the data type object.
Example
print MyWorkerPool.getAssignedWorker(2) 
-- might, for example, return .Resources.John:2
See also
Assigned Workers [WorkerPool]
getAssignedWorker [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3103
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

getAssignedWorkersTable [SimTalk]
Returns the table that contains the assigned Workers of the WorkerPool designated by <Path>.
Syntax
<Path>.getAssignedWorkersTable([AssignedWorkers:table]) -> any
Type
Method
Parameter
The optional parameter AssignedWorkers of data type table designates the name of the table into which
the Workers will be written.
If you do not specify the optional parameter, Plant Simulation returns an array with the assigned Workers.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
Example
MyWorkerPool.getAssignedWorkersTable(MyAssignedWorkersTable)
MyWorkerPool.getAssignedWorkersTable
See also
Assigned Workers [WorkerPool]
getAssignedWorkersTable [SimTalk]
11-3104 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

getIdleWorker [SimTalk]
Returns the first idle Worker in the WorkerPool designated by <Path>.
Remarks
getIdleWorker returns the first idle Worker for whom the attribute IsIdle is to true and sets it to false. When
you no longer need the Worker, you can send the Worker to the WorkerPool and set IsIdle to true.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.getIdleWorker -> object
Return Value
The return value has the data type object.
Is the first idle Worker in the WorkerPool.
VOID if no Worker is idle.
Example
.Resources.WorkerPool.getIdleWorker
SimTalk
IsIdle [SimTalk] - Worker
NumIdleWorkers [SimTalk]
getIdleWorker [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3105
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

getWorkersToCreateTable [SimTalk]
Returns the Workers to Create table of the WorkerPool designated by <Path> and writes it into a table.
Remarks
Plant Simulation always resolves relative paths in relation to the Frame in which the WorkerPool is
inserted. If Plant Simulation cannot resolve a path in the Scope array during the simulation, it shows an
error message and asks if you would like to stop the simulation.
This also applies to the Home Location.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.getWorkersToCreateTable(WorkersToCreateTable:table/void[, byref 
Inherited:boolean])
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter WorkersToCreateTable of data type table designates the name of the table that contains
the Workers to be created. The column of the table has to have the data type table.
If the optional parameter Inherited is passed, you can specify VOID for the parameter
WorkersToCreateTable. In this case WorkersToCreateTable is ignored.
• The optional parameter Inherited designates a local variable of data type boolean which is set to true if
the WorkersToCreateTable of the WorkerPool is inherited. It is set to false if it is not inherited.
Example
var rt: table                             // read the Workers to Create 
table
MyWorkerPool.getWorkersToCreateTable(rt)  // set the new amount
rt [2,1]:= AmountOfWorkers                // name of a Variable
// assign the Workers to Create table to the WorkerPool 
MyWorkerPool.setWorkersToCreateTable(rt)
SimTalk
setWorkersToCreateTable [SimTalk]
getWorkersToCreateTable [SimTalk]
